# Koka 2.6.0 Released { .heading-no-number }

~ begin blog-meta
**December 2023** · Language, Release
~ end blog-meta

---

Koka 2.6.0 introduces first-class constructor contexts and expanded support for fully-in-place (FIP) programming, plus initial VS Code support.

---

## First-Class Constructor Contexts

Koka now supports **first-class constructor contexts**, which significantly improves the efficiency of various standard library functions like `partition`. This technique allows for more efficient recursive data structure manipulation.

## Fully In-Place (FIP)

We have expanded the use of `fip` and `fbip` annotations across `std/core`. These annotations allow the compiler to verify that operations are performed in-place, ensuring performance and memory usage for these functions when used with unique values.

## Initial VS Code Support

Initial language support for VS Code is now available, featuring:
- **Type Information and Go-to Definition**: Navigate and understand your code more easily.
- **Code Lenses**: Run `main`, `test`, or `example` functions directly from the editor.
- **Automatic Installation**: The VS Code extension can now automatically install the latest Koka compiler.

Special thanks to [Tim Whiting](https://github.com/TimWhiting) and [Fredrik Wieczerkowski](https://github.com/fwcd) for all their work on making this possible!

